{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART got 0xd2 want 0xa5 with TRAP uart data mismatch and FAIL 0xdead (refs picosoc/simpleuart.v:20, picosoc/picosoc.v:190). The excerpt has duplicate `0: begin` labels at lines 78 and 83, so recv_state 1 half-bit start wait `if (2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider)` is unreachable and state 1 falls to default full-bit sampling. This half-bit offset corrupts recv_pattern sampling causing the 0xa5->0xd2 mismatch.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -78,9 +78,9 @@
 				0: begin
 					if (!ser_rx)
 						recv_state <= 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
-				0: begin
+				1: begin
 					if (2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_state <= 2;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP: uart data mismatch, loopback 0xa5 matches"}

